# Data and large binary outputs.
# `data/*` rather than `data/`: git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so
# a `!data/file` negation is silently ignored under the `data/` form. With
# `data/*` the small, reviewable provenance CSVs below can be re-included by name
# (the two gate files were previously force-added, which left no record of why
# they were tracked). Everything else under data/ -- h5ad, per-islet CSVs,
# geojson, the 2.65M-row cell_distance.csv -- stays ignored.
data/*
!data/phenotype_gates_per_image.csv
!data/phenotype_gates_provenance.csv
!data/donor_metadata.csv
# Versioned rule definitions are source inputs, not generated assignments.
!data/phenotype_rules.csv
# Referenced from CLAUDE.md as the canonical lineage doc but never actually
# tracked -- the blanket data/ rule kept it out of every clone.
!data/DATA_PROVENANCE.md
# Repo-root QuPath per-compartment means export (11 GB) -- never commit; regenerated by QuPath.
/CellCompartments.tsv
pdfs/
*.pdf
*.Rout
gson/
single_cell_analysis/*.h5ad
single_cell_analysis/*.tsv
app/shiny_app/www/local_images
app/shiny_app/R/00_00_candidate_profile.R
local_images/
app/shiny_app/www/segmentation_data/
AI_Markdown/
analysis_output/*
# Same pattern as data/*: git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a
# !islet_analysis/CLAUDE.md negation is inert under the bare directory form. The
# root CLAUDE.md cites this file as the canonical reference for the Python
# analysis pipeline, but the blanket rule kept it out of every clone. Everything
# else here (h5ad, tsv, png, .venv) stays ignored.
islet_analysis/*
!islet_analysis/CLAUDE.md
literature/*

# Generated analysis/review outputs outside the standard data/ tree.
/reports/
# Hypothesis-testing results (output/<analysis>_<date>/, from 2026-10-22): per-object
# tables, model fits, figures and full-text extractions of the local papers. Each
# folder carries its README, commands and source hashes; the scripts that
# regenerate it are tracked under scripts/research/.
/output/
# Per-run calibration snapshots/bindings contain machine-specific paths and
# scientific evidence. Keep them with the checksummed run, even when a scratch
# run lives outside data/ or output/. The producing Python modules stay tracked.
**/typing/calibration_context.json
**/typing/calibration_context/
**/typing/structure_update.json
**/typing/component_selection.json
**/typing/component_selection_audit.json
*-structure-audit/
# Release/agent-transfer archives; their source and small receipts are tracked.
*.oci.tar
*.git.bundle
*.h5ad
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.parquet
*.arrow
*.feather
*.npy
*.npz
*.zarr/
*.tif
*.tiff
*.TIF
*.TIFF
# Native QuPath projects, object hierarchies and automatic backups.
*.qpproj
*.qpproj.*
*.qpdata
*.qpdata.*
*.geojson
*.geojson.gz
*.gpkg
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# R workspace and environment files
.RData
.Rhistory
app/shiny_app/.Renviron
.Renviron
.Rproj.user/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# Organized script directories (duplicates for organization)
scripts/Python/
scripts/R_files/
scripts/Shell_scripts/

# Notebook execution outputs
notebooks/*_executed.ipynb
notebooks/*.png

# Generated slide decks (outputs/, e.g. Explorer_T1D_Revised_Data_Flow.pptx) and the
# Codex agent's build artifacts for them (renders, layout dumps, candidate decks).
/outputs/
/.codex-artifacts/

# testthat failure snapshots, rewritten on every failing run.
app/shiny_app/tests/testthat/_problems/
app/shiny_app/tests/testthat/testthat-problems.rds

# App runtime flags
app/shiny_app/APP_LOADED_FLAG
app/shiny_app/R/APP_LOADED_FLAG

# Temporary files
tmp/
*.log
*.log.*
*.pid

# Virtual environments and caches
.venv*/
venv*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
# Browser dependencies may be a shared-worktree symlink rather than a directory.
/deploy/browser/node_modules
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Excel and other large source data
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.xlsm

# IDE and local configs
.vscode/
.DS_Store
.~lock.*#

# Tool downloads (large jars)
scripts/tools/

# Large package files
*.deb
*.rpm
scripts/scvi_comparison_results/new_latent_single_cell.npy

# Apptainer/Singularity images (built artifacts, multi-GB)
*.sif
